window.QUOTATION_DATA = {"companies":[{"name":"House Construct","rate":"₹2299/sq ft","total":10110050},{"name":"Sribha Infra Build","rate":"₹2199/sq ft","total":8852342},{"name":"Smart Space Construction","rate":"₹2200/sq ft","total":9762000}],"sections":[{"row":5,"name":"Designs & Drawings","descriptions":["1. Architectural Layout 1 2D / 3D\n2. Structural Design\n3. MEP Drawings\n4. 3D Elevation\n5. Digital site survey\n6. Isometric Drawings Virtual reality","1. 2D Floor Plan\n2. 3D Elevation\n3. Structural Design\n4. Electricl Drawings\n5. Plumbing Drawings\n6. Digital site survey","1. Good for Construction (GFC) architectural floor plans in 2D.  \n2. 2D furniture layout.  \n3. Structural design in accordance with applicable Indian Standards and approved design criteria.  \n4. Soil test and site layout marking using total station.  \n5. Basic 3D front elevation.  \n6. Design revisions: up to limited major planning revisions before design freeze.   \n7. All drawings shall be approved in writing by the client before execution. Working drawings and \nrevision status shall be maintained in a drawing register."]},{"row":7,"name":"Earth Work","descriptions":["1. The Foundation has been assumed as Isolated footings in regular Soil of Bearing Capacity\n180kN/mA2 and above.\n\n2. For soil conditions requiring specialized foundation design Orland additional depth Of\nexcavation additional charges will be applicable.\n\n3. In case Of rocky terrains, excavation cost shall be charged extra for foundation, sump, soak\npit and other excavation at Rs. 35 per cubic feet.\n\n4. Any Soil Bought up 'Carting away will be client Scope.","","SITE PREPARATION, EXCAVATION AND FOUNDATION  \n1. Earthwork excavation shall be carried out manually or by machinery to the dimensions and depths \nrequired by the approved structural drawings.  \n2. Foundation pricing is based on isolated footings in ordinary soil and assumed excavation depth \nup to 6 ft, subject to soil-test findings and structural design.  \n3. Rock excavation, dewatering, shoring, soling, specialised foundations, soil replacement and \nexcavation beyond the stated assumptions shall be additional through a written Variation Order.  \n4. PCC below footings and ground-floor flooring: 100 mm thickness, nominal mix or grade as \nconfirmed by the structural engineer.  \n5. RCC footings, columns and plinth beams: M20 or higher grade as specified in the approved \nstructural design.  \n6. Anti-termite treatment below ground-floor PCC.  \n7. Plinth level: 1 ft 6 in above existing ground level, subject to approved site levels."]},{"row":9,"name":"RCC and MASONARY WORKS","descriptions":["1. RCC Framed Structure in M-20/25 grade Concrete in 20mm & 40mm Aggregates or as\nadvised in the RCC Design Mix as per the Structural designe.\n\n2. The Plinth level will be Provided at a height of 1 feet and 6 inches above the existing Ground Level. PCC of 100mm shall be Provided at the Plinth Level below the Ground floor Flooring.\n\n3. Internal plastering (1:5 Cement mortar) and Ceiling Plastering (1:4 Cement mortar) shall be\ndone by 15 mm thickness .\n\n4. External plastering (1:5 Cement mortar) 1st Coat and (1:3 Cement mortar) in second coat shall be done by total 20 mm thickness .\n\n5. Water proofing compound Of Fosroc/ equivalent brand shall be used in the external plastering.\nand mortar mix used in fixing washroom tiles.\n\n6. Steel - JSW, Indus or equivalent Cement - UltraTech, Birla or equivalent 43 or 53 grade.\n\n7. Chicken mesh shall be used near beams, column & masonry wall junction and at the chasing\nfor electrical conduits.\n\n8. Blockwork Masonry in Standard Solid Concrete Blocks with Plaster as per the design 4\" for\ninternal Partitions and 6\" for External Walls.\n\n9. Height of each floor shall be 10' 6\" from Finished Floor level to Finished Floor level.\n\n10. M-Sand shall be used for Masonry and P-Sand shall be used for Plastering.\n\n11. Cut-Lintels shall be provided only over openings with bearing of Ifeet into the edge of the\nopenings. For providing concrete band all around, additional Charges shall be applicable.\n\n12. Water proofing shall be done in the terrace slab, all washrooms and balconies using Fosroc /\nDr Fixit Brush bond or equivalent brands.\n\n13. In case the Site level is more than 6\" below the Road level, additional filling charges will be\napplicable.SSM below the plinth beam is charged additional.\n\n14. For constrained sites where Materials & excavated soil cannot be stored will have an\nadditional charge.","1. RCC Framed Structure        \na. The building shall be constructed using RCC (Reinforced Cement Concrete) in M20 or \nM25 grade concrete, using 20mm and 40mm aggregates, or as per the RCC design mix \nrecommended by the Structural Engineer.        \nb. The height of each floor shall be 10 feet (10'-0\"), measured from the Finished Floor \nLevel (FFL) of one floor to the FFL of the floor above.        \nc. The internal clear height will be reduced by the thickness of the RCC slab and finished \nflooring.        \n2. Materials Specifications        \na. Cement: ACC, Ramco, or equivalent brands of 43 or 53 Grade cement at Rs. 380/- per \nbag.        \nb. Steel: Indus TMT, Sunvik, A1 Gold, Jindal or equivalent brands at Rs. 68,000/- per MT.        \nc. Steel Consumption: Assumed at 3.0 kg per sqft. Any quantity used beyond this will be \ncharged based on actual consumption, as per the recommendations of the Structural \nDesigner. Labour, Transportation & Binding wire additional charges shall be applicable \non the excess steel.        \nd. Aggregates: 20mm and 40mm graded aggregates as per mix design.        \ne. Sand: M-sand for masonry; P-sand for plastering.        \n3. Blockwork and Masonry        \na. Standard Solid Concrete Blocks to be used.        \nb. 6-inch blocks for external walls, assumed at Rs. 40 (+/-5) per block.        \nc. 4-inch blocks for internal partitions, assumed at Rs. 30 (+/-5) per block.        \nd. Masonry includes internal plastering (1:6), external plastering (1:5), and ceiling \nplastering (1:4).        \ne. Plaster thickness: 15mm internal, and 18mm external.        \n4. Foundation and Site Conditions        \na. Foundation is assumed to be Isolated Footings suitable for regular soil with a bearing \ncapacity of 180 kN/m², and a maximum excavation depth of 5 feet.        \nb. For every 1 foot of additional excavation, Rs. 35/sqft will be charged across the entire \nsite area.        \nc. In rocky terrain, excavation will incur additional charges of Rs. 40 per cubic foot.\n\nd. If the site level is more than 6 inches below road level, additional filling charges will \napply: Rs. 48,000 for 1 foot (for a 30’x40’ site), prorated for other plot sizes.        \ne. For sites where excavated soil cannot be stored on-site, carting out and refilling will \nincur an additional charge of Rs. 2,500 per tractor load (up to 5 km lead).        \n5. Plinth and Substructure        \na. Plinth level will be provided at 1’-6” above existing ground level.        \nb. PCC of 40mm shall be laid at plinth level below the ground floor flooring.        \nc. Any plinth height increase beyond this shall be charged at Rs. 60/sqft for each 6\" \nincrease.        \nd. Size stone masonry (SSM) for plinth height increase shall be charged at Rs. 200/cu.ft.        \n6. Waterproofing and Finishes        \na. Waterproofing for all washrooms shall be carried out using Fosroc / Dr. Fixit Brushbond \nor equivalent.        \nb. Weatherproof course shall be applied on the terrace using Dr. Fixit or equivalent.        \nc. A curing compound such as Sika Antisol or equivalent shall be used on external \nplastered surfaces.        \nd. Chicken mesh shall be provided at the junctions of beam-column and masonry walls, \nand wherever electrical conduit chasing exceeds 2” in depth and width.        \n7. Structural Provisions        \na. Cut Lintels will be provided only over structural openings with 6-inch bearing on either \nside.        \nb. Through Lintels around all walls will be charged at an extra cost of Rs. 350 per running \nfoot, if required or requested.","1. Cement: Ultratech/ ACC/ Ramco or approved equivalent; grade shall be selected according to \nstructural and application requirements.  \n2. Reinforcement steel: A one/ Turbo/Sunvik or approved equivalent; grade Fe500D / Fe550D.  \n3. Commercial steel allowance: 3.0 kg per sq ft. This allowance shall never limit or override the \napproved structural design or safety requirements.  \n4. Any excess or reduction in reinforcement shall be reconciled using approved GFC drawings, bar\nbending schedules, joint records, agreed wastage and the confirmed base rate per MT.  \n5. Concrete grade, cover, curing, formwork, construction joints and de-shuttering shall follow \napproved drawings and quality procedures.  \n6. Concrete mixing method: RMC / Machine Mix / Permitted Site Mix Conditions."]},{"row":11,"name":"UNDERGROUND SUMP","descriptions":["","","A. Underground sump of 8,000 L capacity with 6-inch blockwork, RCC slab and access cover.  \nB. Internal waterproofing, plastering, pipe sleeves and water-holding test shall be included as per the \napproved detail.  \nC. Additional capacity shall be charged at 12 rs/ltr."]},{"row":13,"name":"BLOCKWORK","descriptions":["","","1.  External walls: standard 6-inch solid concrete blocks. \n. Internal partitions: standard 4-inch solid concrete blocks.  \nC. M-sand shall be used for masonry work.  \nD. Floor-to-floor height: 10 ft 6 inch including slab, subject to approved architectural drawings.  \nE. Parapet wall: 4-inch blockwork, 3 ft 6 in high with coping, unless modified by the approved \nelevation."]},{"row":15,"name":"PLASTERING","descriptions":["","","A. Internal plaster: 12 mm average thickness in cement mortar 1:6.  \nB. External plaster: 15 mm average thickness in cement mortar 1:5.  \nC. Ceiling plaster: cement mortar 1:4 where required.  \nD. P-sand shall be used for plastering.  \nE. Chicken mesh shall be fixed at RCC-masonry junctions.  \nF. Surface preparation, curing, line, level and crack-treatment procedures shall be included."]},{"row":17,"name":"WATERPROOFING","descriptions":["","","A. Terrace and toilet waterproofing shall use Dr. Fixit or approved system, with substrate preparation \nand application according to manufacturer recommendations.  \nB. Covered areas shall include terrace, toilets.  \nC. Waterproofing shall be tested by ponding / water-holding test for the agreed period before covering."]},{"row":19,"name":"STAIRCASE AND RAILINGS","descriptions":["","","A. RCC staircase with approved waist slab and structural details.  \nB. Internal and external staircase granite allowance: Rs. 120 per sq ft including GST.  \nC. Internal staircase railing: SS railings without Glass (3 feet height) – 750 Sq ft.   \nD. External staircase railing: MS railings (3 feet height)-150 Sq ft."]},{"row":22,"name":"KITCHEN","descriptions":["1. Ceramic wall tiles will be provided upto 2'-0\" above the Kitchen Counter top Of - upto INR 80\nper Sft Kitchen counter top of width, 2'-0\" in 18mm Granite of - upto INR 200 per Sft is\nincluded.\n\n2. Double layer nosing at the edge in the front has been included along with polishing Single\nbowl Granite Kitchen Sink Of - upto Rs 8000 shall be provided .\n\n3. Kitchen faucet along with accessories of Parryware/Hindware/Jaguar or equivalent make\nshall be provided Any Other Faucet & Accessories - ISI Marked - RS.6000/","1. Kitchen Area and Scope        \na. For every one dwelling unit, one kitchen of up to 80 sq. ft. is included in the base \npackage.        \nb. Additional dwelling units or kitchens exceeding 80 sq. ft. shall be charged on a prorata \nbasis.        \n2. Wall Finishes and Tiling        \na. Ceramic wall tiles will be provided up to 2 feet height above the kitchen countertop, \nat a rate of up to Rs. 50 per sq. ft.     \n\nb. Ceramic tiles for the kitchen backsplash will be of standard make, and any tile selection \nbeyond the specified rate will be chargeable as per actuals.        \n3. Kitchen Countertop        \na. The kitchen slab shall be made of 18mm thick granite, with a 2 feet width, at a rate of \nup to Rs. 160 per sq. ft.        \nb. The granite slab will include a double-layer nosing at the front edge, and polishing is \nincluded in the standard scope.        \n4. Sink and Plumbing Fixtures        \na. A single-bowl stainless steel or Quartz kitchen sink worth up to Rs. 4,000 is included.        \nb. A main kitchen faucet worth up to Rs. 1,800 shall be provided, of Parryware, Hindware, \nJaquar, or equivalent ISI-marked brand.        \nc. Any additional faucets and accessories will be of ISI-certified make and are subject to \ninclusion based on the design.        \n5. Plumbing Provisions        \na. Provision will be made for one water inlet point near the kitchen sink for installation \nof a water purifier, or as per final design.        \nb. One inlet and one outlet point will be provided for a washing machine in the utility \narea or dry balcony, as per the approved design.        \nc. A bib cock of Jaquar or equivalent worth up to Rs. 800 shall be provided in the utility \narea.        \n6. Ventilation        \na. Provision for an exhaust fan shall be included in the kitchen and utility areas as \napplicable.        \nb. Please note that the exhaust fan fixture itself is not included in the standard scope.","1. Kitchen counter: 20 mm granite, basic material allowance Rs. 180 per sq ft including GST.  \n2. Kitchen wall tiles above counter: allowance Rs. 65 per sq ft including GST, height and area \naccording to approved drawings.  \n3. Kitchen sink allowance : Rs 6000 for owner house & Rs 4500 for rent house.  \n4. Kitchen faucet: Rs. 2500 for owner house & Rs 1800 for rent house.  \n5. One water-purifier inlet point and exhaust-fan provision per approved kitchen layout.  \n6. Modular kitchen cabinets, shutters, baskets, appliances and interior works are excluded unless \nseparately quoted."]},{"row":24,"name":"Bathroom PLUMBING AND SANITARY","descriptions":["1. Ceramic wall tiles will be provided upto 7 '-On above the Finished Floor Level Of\nper Sft.Bathroom Flooring - Anti-skid tiles Of value upto Rs. 70/- per sqft.\n\n2. Spacer joints shall be provided in the floor tiles and the wall dado tiles.\n- upto INR 80\n\n3. Grouting shall be Of polymeric cement grout Of Roff/ Weber/ equivalent brands.\n\n4. Sewer line connection to the main drain line is included in the package up to 20 feet from the\nbuilding.\n\n5. External pipes shall be fixed on raised clamps.\n\n6. CPVC Pipe - Ashirwad/Supreme or equivalent\n\n7. Bathroom doors - Waterproof flush doors with IO years warranty.\n\n8. Geyser & Solar provisions are included.\n\n9. Sanitary ware and CP fittings of - upto INR 80,000 are included per 1000 sft of Package Built\nUp area.\n\n10. Additional Sanitary Ware and CP Fittings will be charged on a Pro-Rata Basis. One number\nEWC, Health Faucet, Wash Basin, Basin Mixer, Overhead Shower with 2 in 1 Shower wall Mixer\nOf Hindware [Parryware make is included\n\n11. Plumbing shall be carried out in CPVC Pipes Of Ashirwad /Supreme or Equivalent Make.","1. Bathroom Allocation        \na. One bathroom is included per 500 sq. ft. of package built-up area.        \nb. Any additional bathrooms required shall be charged on a pro-rata basis.        \n2. Wall and Floor Finishes        \na. Ceramic wall tiles shall be provided up to a height of 7’-0” above Finished Floor Level, \nat a value of up to Rs. 50 per sq. ft.        \nb. Anti-skid floor tiles for bathrooms are included, at a value of up to Rs. 50 per sq. ft.        \nc. Spacer joints shall be provided for both floor and wall tiles.       \n\nd. Grouting shall be done using cementitious grout of Roff or equivalent brand.        \ne. Gratings shall be properly sealed using cementitious grout of Roff or equivalent.        \n3. Rainwater Drainage        \na. Two 6-inch rainwater discharge pipes shall be provided per 1000 sq. ft. of plot area.        \nb. Any additional rainwater pipes required will be charged on a pro-rata basis.        \n4. Sewer Line and Drainage        \na. Connection of the sewer line to the main drainage line is included for up to 10 feet \nfrom the building.        \nb. Road cutting, permissions, and related municipal charges are not included and shall \nbe borne by the client.        \nc. All external drainage pipes shall be installed using raised clamps for secure fixing.        \n5. Sanitary Ware and CP Fittings        \na. Sanitary ware and CP fittings worth up to Rs. 50,000 per 1000 sq. ft. of package builtup \narea are included, from brands such as Cera or equivalent.     \nb. Inclusions per bathroom:     \n• One floor-mounted EWC      \n• One health faucet     \n• One wash basin     \n• One basin mixer     \n• One overhead shower     \n• One 2-in-1 shower wall mixer (All of Jaquar, Hindware, Parryware, or \nequivalent make)         \nc. Any additional sanitary ware or CP fittings beyond the standard scope shall be    charged \non a pro-rata basis.        \n6. Plumbing Works        \na. All internal and external plumbing work shall be done using CPVC pipes of Astral or \nequivalent make.        \nb. Piping will follow the layout and specifications as per the final plumbing design.        \n7. Ventilation        \na. Provision for exhaust fan installation shall be made in all bathrooms.        \nb. Please note: the exhaust fan fixture itself is not included in the base scope.","A. CPVC / PVC pipes and fittings: Finolex / Ashirvad or approved equivalent.  \nB. Pipe classes, diameters and hot/cold-water scope shall be according to approved plumbing \ndrawings.  \nC. Sanitary ware and CP fittings allowance: Rs. 35,000 per Bathroom (only 2 bathrooms per floor) \nD. Rainwater discharge pipes and ground-floor inspection chambers shall be provided as per \napproved drawings.  \nE. Plumbing pressure tests and drainage-flow tests shall be recorded before concealment.  \nF. Pump, auto-starter, water-level controller and borewell equipment are owner scope unless \nseparately quoted.  \nG. Water-supply pressure tests, drainage-flow tests and leakage checks shall be recorded before \nconcealment."]},{"row":27,"name":"Doors & Windows","descriptions":["1. Windows shall be Sal wood/3 Track Premium UPVC Of gauge 92mm Of - Rs. 800 per Sft With 2\nGlass and 1 mesh shutters, including all fixtures and fittings\n\n2. Window Grills Of upto INR 160 per sft shall be provided Of 12mm thick MS rods with maximum\nspacing 100mm between rods in either direction.\n\n3. The main door shall be 32mm thick of Size 3'6\"X7' of - upto Rs 60,000 including frame in\nTeak or equivalent. Including fixtures.\n\n4. Pooja room door - Teak door with fixtures & polish upto Rs. 30,000 shall be provided.lnternal\nDoors shall be 32mm thick Membrane/Flush doors of Size 3'O\"X7' of - upto Rs 11,000\nincluding frame in Honne Wood. Including fixtures.\n\n5. Bathroom Doors shall be 32mm thick Waterproof Flush doors Of Size 2 '6\" XT Of - upto Rs\n8,000 including frame in Sal wood. Including fixtures.","Doors, Windows, and Ventilators\n\n1. Windows and Ventilators        \na. The total area of openings for windows and ventilators, including frames, is assumed \nat 10% of the package built-up area.        \nb. Any additional window or ventilator area beyond this limit shall be charged on a \nprorata basis.        \nc. Windows shall be UPVC sliding windows (3-track with 1 mesh track) made from Jindal \nProfiles, valued at up to Rs. 420 per sq. ft., inclusive of glass shutters and mosquito \nmesh shutters.        \nd. Window grills shall be provided at a cost of up to Rs. 210 per sq. ft., made of 10mm \nthick MS rods, with maximum spacing of 125mm between rods in both directions. The \ngrills shall be finished with enamel paint.        \ne. Chajjas (sunshades) shall be provided above all windows with 1-foot outward \nprojection and 6-inch bearing on each side of the window.      \n2. Main Door        \na. One main door shall be provided per dwelling unit, or for every 1000–1500 sq. ft. of \npackage built-up area.        \nb. The main door shall be a 32mm African Teak door or equivalent of size 3’-6” x 7’, \nvalued up to Rs. 40,000 including the frame, made of African Teak or equivalent.   \nc. The main door specification includes:        \n• 2 brass tower bolts     \n• 3 brass hinges      \n• 1 Europa/Godrej lock (up to Rs. 2,000)     \n• 1 wall-mounted magnetic door stopper        \nd. Pooja door shall be a 32mm African Teak door or equivalent of size 3’x 7’, valued up   \nto Rs. 20,000 including the frame, made of African Teak or equivalent.        \n3. Internal Doors        \na. Internal doors shall be 32mm thick membrane or flush doors, of size 3’-0” x 7’, valued \nup to Rs. 15,000 including frame, made of Sal wood with frame size 5” x 3”.    \nb. Internal door hardware includes:        \n• 2 MS/SS tower bolts    \n• 3 MS/SS hinges, 1 wall-mounted magnetic door stopper","A. Main door: teak frame 6 in x 4 in, 32 mm shutter with fittings, basic allowance Rs. 50,000 per \ncomplete set. (Only 1 set per floor) \nB. Pooja door: teak frame 5 in x 3 in, 32 mm shutter with fittings, basic allowance Rs. 28,000 per \ncomplete set. (Only 1 set per floor) \nC. Internal door: mahogany / sal frame with 32 mm shutter and fittings, basic allowance Rs. 11,000 \nper complete set, subject to approved schedule. \nD. Bathroom WPC door: basic allowance Rs. 8,000 per complete set as per Package.   \nE. Door dimensions, quantities, hardware models and polishing specification shall follow the \napproved door schedule.  \nF. Main and pooja door polish: Hand melamine polish at Rs. 140 per sq ft."]},{"row":29,"name":"WINDOWS","descriptions":["","","A. UPVC 2.5 track windows with glass & mesh, basic allowance Rs 450 per Sqft.  \nB. Glass thickness 4mm. Upvc profile series, reinforcement, hardware. mesh type, sealant.  \nC. MS window grills using 12MM rods, Basic allowance Rs 140 per Sqft, including fabrication, \nanticorrosive primer & enamel finish.  \nD. Window sizes and quantities shall be according to the approved window schedule."]},{"row":32,"name":"PAINTING AND POLISH","descriptions":["1. The exteriors will be painted with one coat Asian Primer and two coats Of Apex Exterior\nEmulsion weatherproof paint or equivalent.\n\n2. The interior walls and Ceiling shall be painted with 2 coats Birla Putty and 2 coats Latest\nApcolite Emulsion or equivalent.\n\n3. All MS Steel grills and railings shall be painted with an anti corrosion coat with a final coat Of\nEnamel Paint.\n\n4. Interior Painting - Birla Putty 2 Coat + Latest Apcolite Emulsion or equivalent 2 Coats.\n\n5. Exterior Painting - 1 Coat Asian Primer + Apex Exterior Emulsion weatherproof Paint or\nequivalent 2 Coats.","Painting Works\n\nInterior Painting Works       \na. Application of 2 coats of Asian Wall Putty for surface leveling and smoothness.       \nb. Application of 1 coat of Asian Primer for proper adhesion and surface preparation.       \nc. Application of 2 coats of Asian Paints Tractor Shyne Emulsion for a clean, uniform interior \nfinish.       \nExterior Painting Works       \na. Application of 1 coat of Asian Primer to ensure strong adhesion and weather protection.      \n\nb. Application of 2 coats of Apex Exterior Emulsion for long-lasting, durable exterior \nprotection and finish.","A. Internal walls and ceilings: two coats putty, one coat primer and two coats Latest Premium \nemulsion by Asian / Nippon.  \nB. External walls: one coat primer and two coats Apex weatherproof paint by Asian / Nippon.  \nC. MS grills and railings: anticorrosive primer and enamel finish.  \nD. Main and pooja door polish shall be as finally confirmed in the material schedule.  \nE. Client shall approve colour samples. Additional colours, textures or premium finishes beyond the \npackage shall be chargeable."]},{"row":34,"name":"Flooring","descriptions":["1. Living and Dining room flooring shall be in Vitrified Tiles or Granite of - upto INR 160 per sft\nOther Rooms and Kitchen flooring shall be in Vitrified Tiles or Granite of - upto INR 120 per sft.\n\n2. Staircase flooring shall be in Lapotra Granite of - upto INR 120 per sft.\n\n3.Parking area flooring shall be in Anti-skid tiles of - upto INR 90 per sft.\n\n4. Balconies and open areas shall be in Anti-skid tiles of - upto INR 90 per sft\n\n4. Terrace tiles shall be additionally charged Skirting shall be of matching Vitrified Tiles or\nGranite not less than 75mm high.\n\n5. Ceramic tiles for walls shall be free from cracks, spots, grazes, chipped edges and corners.\n\n6. Variation in size shall be limited to +1- 1.5mm. Thickness shall be specified, but in no case\nshall they be less than 6 mm.\n\n7. Granite if used shall be hard, sound, free from cracks, cavities, holes, patches of injurious\nveins, weathered portions, flaws, etc.\n\n8. Granite used should have a minimum thickness Of 19 mm Additional charges shall be\napplicable for laying Italian marble of upto INR 75 per sft.\n\n9. Over and above the laying charges, an additional chemical treatment charge of INR 30 per sft\nshall be applicable.","Flooring and Wall Finishes  \n\n1. Flooring Materials        \na. Living and Dining Rooms shall be finished with 2' x 4' vitrified tiles, Granite valued up \nto Rs. 100 per sq. ft.        \nb. Bedrooms and Kitchen flooring shall be in 2' x 4' vitrified tiles, also valued up to Rs. 80 \nper sq. ft.        \nc. Staircase flooring shall be provided in Sadderahalli granite, valued up to Rs. 85 per sq. \nft.        \nd. Parking area flooring shall be laid in anti-skid tiles, valued up to Rs. 45 per sq. ft.        \ne. Balconies and open areas shall also be laid with anti-skid tiles valued up to Rs. 45 per \nsq. ft.        \nf. Terrace tiling is not included in the base package and shall be charged additionally.        \n2. Skirting and Wall Dado        \na. Skirting shall be provided using matching vitrified tiles or granite, with a minimum \nheight of 100mm.       \n\nb. Wall dado in toilets shall be provided using 2’ x 2’ ceramic tiles, valued up to Rs. 50per \nsq. ft.        \n3. Tile and Granite Installation Standards        \na. Wall tiles shall be fixed using tile adhesive, and joints shall be cleaned and grouted with \nsite-made cementitious grout of Roff, Weber, or equivalent brands.        \nb. All ceramic wall tiles must be free from cracks, spots, grazes, chipped edges, and \ncorner damage.        \nc. Variation in tile size shall be within ±1.5mm, and tile thickness shall not be less than   \n6mm.        \nd. All flooring, dado, and skirting must be laid level and to plumb.        \ne. Grouting for balcony and terrace tiles (if opted) shall be done with cementitious grout \nfrom Roff or equivalent.        \n4. Granite Specifications        \na. Granite used shall be hard, sound, and free from cracks, cavities, patches, weathered \nportions, and flaws.        \nb. The minimum thickness of granite shall be 19mm.        \nc. Labour charges for cutting, laying, polishing, nosing, and chamfering of granite are \nchargeable additionally.        \n5. Additional Charges        \na. Laying of Indian marble shall incur an additional charge of up to Rs. 70 per sq. ft.        \nb. Laying of granite shall be charged additionally at Rs. 18 per sq. ft., with an extra Rs. 40 \nper running ft for buffing, chamfering, or nosing where applicable.        \nc. Laying of Italian marble shall be chargeable up to Rs. 90 per sq. ft., with an additional \nchemical treatment charge of Rs. 35 per sq. ft.","A. Living, dining, kitchen and bedrooms: vitrified tiles, basic material allowance Rs. 110 per sq ft \nincluding GST.  \nB. Balcony, sit-out and passage: anti-skid tiles, basic allowance Rs. 55 per sq ft including GST.  \nC. Toilet floor and wall dado: anti-skid / ceramic tiles, basic allowance Rs. 65 per sq ft including \nGST upto 8’ height .  \nD. Parking: anti-skid tiles, basic allowance Rs. 55 per sq ft including GST.  \nE. Pooja wall tiles: basic allowance Rs. 60 per sq ft including GST upto 8’.  \nF. Staircase granite: basic allowance Rs. 120 per sq ft including GST.  \nH.  Cladding tiles: basic allowance Rs. 60 per sqft upto 100sqft per Floor."]},{"row":36,"name":"Electrical","descriptions":["1. Wires - Fireproof wires by Finolex/Havells.\n\n2. Switches & Sockets - GM Modular/Legrand.\n\n3. The electrical points shall be provided as per the Electrical drawings provided.\n\n4. Living/Dining/Family Room shall be provided with 2 numbers fan Point, 4 numbers Light Point,\n4 numbers 5Amp Switch and Sockets and 1 number TV Cable Point .\n\n5. Other Rooms shall be provided with 3 numbers of light points, 1 number of fan point, 4\nnumbers of 5Amp switch and socket in the TV/Study or dresser area as the case may be as\nper design and 1 number 16Amp switch and socket for air conditioning.\n\n6. Kitchen shall be provided with 2 numbers of light points, 5 numbers of 5/15Amp (as the case\nmay be based on Appliance Specifications) switch and socket one each for refrigerator,\nmixer/grinder, oven, water purifier and one above the Kitchen platform.\n\n7. 1 number calling bell shall be provided. More call bell points per dwelling Unit shall be charged\nadditionally.\n\n8. Bathroom shall be provided with 2 numbers of light point, 1 number of geyser point, 3 number\nof 5Amp Switch and Socket near the wash basin.\n\n9. 1 number light point each shall be provided with a two way switch connection for each room,\nlivingroom and staircase.\n\n10. Corridor/passage/portico/parking/utility/terrace/external stairs/balcony/space around\nhouse/any other built up area shall be provided with 8 numbers light points and 8 numbers\n5Amp switches and sockets at suitable locations per 1000 sqft of package built up area.\n\n11. One MCB board of Anchor/Finolex or equivalent make shall be provided Main panel board\nshall be in the Owner's scope including road cutting charges and main-line from pole to panel\nboard.\n\n12.External electrification, AC provision, UPS points and Electric charging points are included .\n\n13. External electrification, AC provision, UPS points and Electric charging points are included","Electrical Works    \n\n1. Wiring and Cabling        \na. All internal wiring shall be done using wires of Finolex silver or equivalent ISI-marked \nbrand.        \nb. Wiring for UPS (if required) shall be charged additionally and is not included in the \nstandard scope.  \nc. All internal Pipe shall be done using pipe of VIP or equivalent.  \n2. Switches and Accessories        \na. Switches and sockets shall be of Hi-Fi, GM Basic or equivalent, as per the approved \nelectrical design.        \nb. One MCB distribution board of IndoAsian or equivalent make shall be provided for \neach dwelling unit.        \n3. Point Distribution by Area        \na. Living / Dining / Family Room shall include:        \n• 2 fan points    \n• 4 light points      \n• 4 numbers of 5 Amp switches and sockets     \n• 1 TV cable point        \nb. Bedrooms / Other Rooms shall include:        \no 3 light points     \no 1 fan point     \no 4 numbers of 5 Amp switch and sockets (located in TV/study/dresser area as \napplicable)  \no 1 number of 16 Amp switch and socket for air conditioning        \nc. Kitchen shall include:        \no 2 light points        \no 5 switch and socket combinations of 5/15 Amp ratings (based on appliance \nspecifications) For: Refrigerator, Mixer/Grinder, Microwave     \nOven, Water Purifier, and one point above the kitchen platform       \n\nd. Bathroom shall include:        \n• 2 light points      \n• 1 geyser point      \nCalling Bell      \n• 1 number of 5 Amp switch and socket near the wash basin       \ne. \n• 1 number calling bell point per dwelling unit is included.    \nWWW.SRIBHAINFRA.COM \n• Any additional calling bell points shall be charged additionally.            \nf. \nTwo-Way Switches        \no Each bed room and staircase will be provided with 1 number light point connected \nto a two-way switch.        \ng. \nOther Areas        \no Corridors, passages, portico, parking, utility, terrace, balconies, external stairs, \nand any additional built-up areas will include: 5 light points and 5 numbers of 5 Amp \nswitches and sockets per 1000 sq.   \nft. of package built-up area.        \n4. Earthing and Panel Board        \na. One earthing provision shall be included per 1000 sq. ft. of package built-up area.        \nThe main panel board, along with road cutting permissions and main-line connection \nfrom the pole to the panel, shall be in the owner's scope and is not included in the \nbase package.","A. Fire-retardant wires: Anchor/Finolex silver or approved equivalent.  \nB. Switches and sockets: Anchor Roma / GM, white finish.  \nC. Main DB and MCB: IndoAsian or approved equivalent.  \nD. Geyser points: all bathrooms.  \nE. AC provision: all bedrooms.  \nF. Main electrical panel, service cable, meter, authority charges and permanent connection are owner \nscope unless expressly included.  \nG. Wire sizes shall match circuit load and an earthing conductor shall be provided in all required \ncircuits. \nH. Electrical continuity, insulation resistance, polarity, phase and earthing tests shall be completed \nbefore handover.  \nI. \nMain incoming panel, meter, service cable, road cutting, authority connection and external \nearthing are not included in package."]},{"row":38,"name":"OVERHEAD TANK AND ACCESS","descriptions":["","","A. Overhead tank: Ganga / Kaveri Triple-layered, 2,000 L, allowance rate Rs. 9 per L.  \nB. Additional capacity shall be charged at the confirmed rate Rs 9 per L.  \nC. MS ladder allowance: Rs. 15,000 according to Package."]},{"row":40,"name":"FABRICATION AND MISCELLANEOUS WORKS","descriptions":["","","A. CNC, cast-iron, complex railing designs and decorative metalwork are additional.  \nB. Septic tank, soak pit, additional lofts, gutter covers and chapadi-stone work shall be quoted            \nseparately with quantities and units.  \nC. Rock excavation, dewatering, additional filling, external staircase headroom, marble laying            \nand special nosing shall be governed by the additional-work schedule.      \nD. Debris shifting will \nbe charged extra.  \nE.       \nF.      \nAdditional lofts may be provided at a charged of – Rs 300/sqft  \nRain water harvesting is additional and shall be provided as per BBMP norms at Rs 25,000"]},{"row":46,"name":"IO. Miscellaneous","descriptions":["1. Overhead Tank - Sintex Double Layered 2500 Itrs.\n\n2. Platform for the OHT shall be charged additional based on the design. Underground sump Of -\n100001- shall be provided with Concrete block masonry.\n\n3. The inside of the wall shall be provided with chicken mesh plastering.\n\n4. MS cover plate Of dimension 600 mm x 600 mm shall be provided. Water Proofing chemical\nbe applied to mortar for plastering.\n\n5. A Septic tank in blockwork, if applicable shall be charged at 12/Ltrs. For RCC septic tank\nadditional charges 20/Ltrs. shall be applicable.\n\n6. Anti-Termite treatment will be provided.\n\n7. Staircase Railing - A simple pattern Staircase Railing shall be in SS With Glass Of - upto Rs.\n900 per Rft for material, painting, welding, fixing, and finishing .\n\n8. Gates shall be charged additional\n\n9. Compound Wall shall be charged additional. If required additional, the compound wall shall be\nin solid cement block masonry with 5 feet height from the ground level and 115 mm in\nthickness. Buttress/columns shall be provided for every IO feet length Of the compound.\n\n10. Expansion joints may be provided wherever necessary. The compound wall shall be\nconstructed on size stone masonry foundation of minimum thickness 450mm and minimum\ndepth 2 feet .\n\n11. The foundation shall be laid on compacted hard soil.\n\n12. Bed concrete Of minimum thickness 80mm shall be provided below the foundation.\nCompound wall shall be plastered and painted as per the plastering and painting\nspecifications.\n\n13. Parapet wall shall be in Blockwork and shall be provided to a height Of 3 feet and 150mm\nthickness. Buttresses shall be provided at every IO feet of length.\n\n14. Balcony and Utility railings along with the Terrace parapet railings if opted above 3 feet\ncharged additional.\n\n15. Elevation Of the building on all sides shall include basic plastering and external painting with\nno other aesthetic elements like cladding, pergola, etc\n\n16. Weather proof course shall be provided at terrace with one coat of waterproofing agent of Dr.\nFixit brand or equivalent.\n\n17. Rain water harvesting is included and shall be provided as per BBMP norms at - INR 20,000\nBarrication around the site during construction in simple shade net is included.\n\n18. Additional charges shall apply for any other kind of Barrication.\n\n19. An Additional capacity Sintex Double layered overhead tank shall be chargeable at INR 9 per\nL.\n\n20. Observation: Post site cleaning exact site level can be determined.\n\n21. Any work done to raise the plinth height or even out the floor levels will be charged on\nactuals.\n\n22. If there are any constraints in material delivery or stocking place and materials to be order in\nsmall quantities, it will be charged on actuals.\n\n23. Site dimension may vary as per the site condition post demolition. Any variations in the slab\narea will checked during execution and it will be charged on actuals.\n\n24. 10.5\" celiling Height (FFL-FFL).\n\n25. Basic Cost Of Cement -Rs 400/ Bag (Ultratech).\n26. Basic Cost of steel -Rs 68/Kg (JSW or equivalent)\n27. Basic Cost of 6\" Block -Rs 40 /Nos.\n28. Basic Cost Of Block -Rs 32/Nos\n\n29. RMC Basic Cost -RS 4600/Cum\n30. Interiors,Seating, planter box, landscaping etc show in the floor plan is not included in the\ncosting.\n\n31. Railings, grills and Windowsarea are considered at 10% Of Total built up area.\n\n32. Steel in the package is assumed at 2.9kg per sft (Any steel quantity over and above this will\nbe chargeable as per actuals based on the recommendations provided by the Structural\ndesigner)\n\n33. Tile laying and adhesive required for the size of above 2'x4' will be chargable as per actuals.\n\n34. Post the structural design, any additional structural components (such as eccentric footing,\nfloating columns, number of columns and column size etc) to be provided for execution of\ndesired floor plan and elevation, it will be charged on actuals.\n\n35. The schedule Of the project depends on location Of the site and also if there is any restrictions\nin the layout","Miscellaneous Provisions\n\n1. Water Storage        \na. Overhead Tank (OHT): A 1500-litre double-layered tank of Apollo make is included.        \no Any additional capacity shall be chargeable at Rs. 10 per litre.        \no Platform for OHT shall be charged additionally as per design.        \nb. Underground Sump: 8000-litre sump is included, constructed in concrete block \nmasonry with:      \n• PCC bed of minimum 125mm thickness     \n• Chicken mesh plastering on inner walls      \n• 600mm x 600mm MS Sump cover plate     \n• Waterproofing chemical mixed in plaster     \n\n• Additional capacity shall be charged at Rs. 13 per litre    \n• RCC sump (if opted) shall be charged cost at Rs. 23 per litre over base    \n2. Staircase Railing        \na. Simple MS railing for the staircase is included up to 10% of the built-up area per 1000 \nsq. ft., at Rs. 300 per sq. ft. (includes material, painting, welding, and fixing). b. \nAdditional staircases or railings on both sides shall be charged extra.        \n3. Gates and Compound Wall        \n• Main gate shall be charged additional, made of Mild Steel with MS posts as per        \napproved design      \n• Shall include 2 hinges per shutter and 1 top and bottom latch  \n4. Compound wall, if opted for, shall be in solid cement block masonry, 5 feet high and \n115mm thick, with:        \n• Buttress/columns every 10 feet        \n• Expansion joints where required        \n• Size stone masonry foundation (450mm wide, 2 feet deep)        \n• 80mm bed concrete, plastering, and painting as per project specs        \n• Compound wall shall be charged additional   \n5. Parapet and Railings        \na. Parapet wall shall be constructed in blockwork, 3 feet in height and 150mm thick, with \nbuttresses every 10 feet.        \nBalcony, utility, and terrace parapet railings (if opted) in MS shall be charged at Rs. \n300 per sq. ft.        \no Complex railing designs shall be charged additionally as per specifications        \n6. Other Provisions        \na. Elevation of the building includes basic plastering and external painting only, with no \ncladding, grooves, projections, pergolas, or aesthetic elements included unless \nspecified.        \nb. Anti-termite treatment shall be charged at Rs. 16 per sq. ft., if required.        \nc. Rainwater Harvesting (7 ft. depth, rings installation, aggregate bed) shall be provided \nas per BBMP norms at Rs. 25,000 per unit.        \nd. Staircase headroom for external staircases shall be charged at par with the package \nbuilt-up area.        \ne. Site barricading during construction using shade net is not included.        \n\nAdditional Charges and Exclusions   \n1. Foundations and Substructure        \na. Size Stone Masonry (SSM) below plinth is not included in the standard package.        \no If required, SSM shall be charged additionally based on site conditions and design \nrequirements.        \n2. Drainage and Access Structures        \na. External Drain Covers made of natural stone (100mm width) shall be provided at Rs.    \n300 per sq. ft.        \nb. In the case of external staircases, the staircase headroom is not included in the \nstandard scope and shall be charged at par with the package built-up area.        \n3. Lofts and Storage        \na. Lofts in rooms and kitchen are not part of the base package.        \no Lofts shall be charged at Rs. 350 per sq. ft.","A. Underground sump of 8,000 L capacity with 6-inch blockwork, RCC slab and access cover.  \nB. Internal waterproofing, plastering, pipe sleeves and water-holding test shall be included as per the \napproved detail.  \nC. Additional capacity shall be charged at 12 rs/ltr."]},{"row":48,"name":"OWNERS SCOPE","descriptions":["","","A. All Governments charges like BESCOM, BWSSB etc.  \nB. Electrical Panel board, Earthing, Road cutting charges, Cabling, Temporary meter & Permanent \nmeter  \nC. Lift Erection & lift cabling.  \nD. Elevation of the building on all sides shall include basic plastering and external painting with no \ncladding or any other aesthetic elements like cladding, pergola, etc  \nE. Interior works like false ceiling, wardrobes, Modular Kitchen, TV unit, POP works, any         \ndecorative works.  \nF. Electrical fittings like bulbs, fans etc. \nG. Monthly electricity bills up to construction.  \nH. Water supply will be borne by the owner up to ending of construction.  \nI. \nProvision of CCTV Points, UPS points and fixing of CCTV equipment’s will be Owner’s          \nscope.  \nJ. Main door & Pooja door Frame Carvings.  \nK. Soil shifting from Site to Outside or Soil purchasing from Outside to Site will be Owner’s          \nScope.  \nL. Passage, Staircase & Lift Wall Cladding.  \nM. Chejja Projection for Front elevation will chargeable on pro-rata basis.  \nN. Gas Pipe Line Connection.  \nO. Water Level Controller – Auto Starter and Submergible Pump.  \nP. Labor Shed Place Provision Will be Owners Scope."]},{"row":50,"name":"CUSTOMIZATION COST","descriptions":["","","A. In case of rocky terrains, excavation cost shall be charged extra for foundation, sump, soak                 \npit and other excavation at Rs. 35 per cubic feet  \nB. In case the Site level is more than 6\" below the Road level, additional filling charges will be               \napplicable at Rs. 50,000 for 600cft plot size   \nC. The Plinth level will be provided at a height of 1 feet and 6 inches above the existing Ground               \nLevel. PCC of 100mm shall be Provided at the Plinth Level below the Ground floor. Any                \nincrease in height of the Plinth thereafter shall be chargeable at Rs. 50,000 for 600cft.  \nD. SSM below plinth is not part of package  \nE. In case of external Staircase headroom is not part of the package. Headroom is chargeable                 \nas  per buit up area.  \nF. Italian Marble Laying, chemical treatment and polishing will be 150/sft.  \nG. Additional cost of laying granite is Rs 23/sft extra. If Buffing or Chamfering/nosing is                  \nencountered half nosing will be 35/RFT, Full Nosing 60/RFT.      \nH.   Chain type staircase will \ncharge - 2000 rupees each step.  \nH. Compound Wall shall be charged additional. If required additional, the compound wall shall                \nbe in solid cement block masonry with 5 feet height from the ground level and 115 mm in             \nthickness. Buttress/columns shall be provided for every 10 feet length of the compound.             \nExpansion joints may be provided wherever necessary. The compound wall shall be             \nconstructed on size stone masonry foundation of minimum thickness 450mm and minimum             \ndepth 2 feet. The foundation shall be laid on compacted hard soil. Bed concrete of minimum             \nthickness 80mm shall be provided below the foundation. Compound wall shall be plastered             \nand painted as per the plastering and painting specifications. Compound wall with Main MS               \ngate  shall be charged at Rs. 1800 per running feet.  \nI. \nChain type staircase will charge – 2500 rs per step"]},{"row":52,"name":"SITE SURVEY AND SETTING OUT","descriptions":["","","A. \nBuilding grids, permanent reference benchmarks and finished-floor levels shall be established \nusing total station or another approved survey instrument.  \nB. Any discrepancy in plot corners, legal boundaries or dimensions supplied by the Owner shall be \nreported before commencement. SSC shall not be responsible for errors in legal-boundary \ninformation supplied by the Owner.  \nC. Finished-floor level shall be finalised considering road level, drainage, approved plan and site \nconditions.  \nD. \nShoring, underpinning or special protection required because of neighbouring structures shall \nbe separately assessed unless expressly included."]},{"row":54,"name":"ADDITIONAL FOUNDATION AND RCC TECHNICAL CONTROLS","descriptions":["","","A. \nSoil investigation shall identify safe bearing capacity, soil strata, groundwater condition, \nrecommended foundation type, indicative foundation depth and settlement considerations.  \nB. Quotation foundation basis: isolated footings in ordinary soil, no continuous dewatering, no rock \nexcavation and no specialised foundation, subject to 6’ depth and the approved structural design.  \nC. Rock excavation, dewatering, shoring, underpinning, raft or pile foundation, soil stabilization, soil \nreplacement, excavation beyond the assumed depth, off-site disposal and imported filling are \nadditional.  \nD. \nExcavation dimensions and depth shall be jointly recorded before PCC, backfilling or \nconcealment.  \nE. Backfilling shall be placed in controlled layers with watering and compaction. Compaction testing \nshall be undertaken where technically required and commercially approved.  \nF. Reinforcement inspection shall verify bar diameter, spacing, laps, anchorage, development length, \ncover, chairs, stirrups, beam-column junctions, openings and embedded sleeves.  \nG. \nConcrete work shall include controlled batching, approved mix, slump testing, cube testing, \nmechanical vibration, construction-joint treatment, curing and pour records.  \nH. \nConcrete cover shall follow the approved drawings and exposure conditions. Cover blocks shall \nbe of approved concrete grade or proprietary type.  \nI. MEP conduits and sleeves shall be coordinated before concreting.   \nJ. Formwork shall be line- and level-checked, adequately supported and sufficiently tight to prevent \ngrout leakage. De-shuttering shall follow approved strength and timing requirements.  \nK. \nHoneycombing and surface defects shall be inspected and repaired using an approved method.  \nL. Steel reconciliation shall use approved GFC drawings, bar-bending schedules, theoretical \nquantities, joint records and the confirmed base rate per MT.  \nM. Concrete supply method shall be Confirm Rmc / Machine Mix / Restricted Site Mix Conditions."]},{"row":119,"name":"MEASUREMENT METHOD","descriptions":["","","1. Building floor area shall be measured separately from compound wall, parapet, sump, external works \nand lump-sum items.  \n2. Each floor shall be jointly measured from approved GFC drawings and actual executed dimensions.  \n3. Measurement sheets shall identify enclosed area, parking, staircase, lift shaft, balcony, utility, terrace, \nheadroom, ducts, chajjas, pergolas and double-height areas separately.  \n4. Any increase or decrease shall be adjusted at the applicable category rate after written approval.  \n5. Compound wall shall be measured only in running feet"]},{"row":121,"name":"PAYMENT CONTROLS","descriptions":["","","1. Each stage payment shall be raised after measurable completion, stage certification and issue of the \napplicable invoice.  \n2. Any disputed portion shall be identified in writing; undisputed certified amounts shall remain \npayable.  \n3. Extra work and upgrades shall be billed separately under approved Variation Orders.  \n4. Delayed payment beyond the agreed cure period may entitle SSC to suspend affected work and \nrecover documented remobilization cost, subject to the final construction agreement."]},{"row":123,"name":"Terms & Conditions","descriptions":["","","1. The Construction commencement date shall be considered the date on which site excavation \nworks begins. Construction period will be 11-13 Months from the date of agreement made \nbetween Client and SSC.   \n2. Payment will be made as per Payment schedule.  \n3. If Payment from Client is delayed then project completion time will vary.  \n4. If any bank loan is delay then project completion time will vary depends on time taken by bank.  \n5. Mentioned budget is inclusive of materials & labours.  \n6. Mentioned budget only for the above-mentioned work and any extra work will charge     \naccordingly.   \n7. All the designs to be approved and signed by the client before start of work.  \n8. No changes will be made after work completion, if any changes made by client, then extra amount \nwill be charged for materials and labour.  \n9. The above-mentioned budget is not inclusive of interior works like false ceiling, wardrobe, \nkitchen unit, TV unit, POP works, any decorative work etc.  \n10. The rates in the schedule are based on the basic rates of finishing materials like Flooring, \nPlumbing, painting etc., if client choose higher rate than the difference amount should be paid \ndirectly to the vendor at the time of purchase.  \n11. Payment schedule & terms will be given to client before start of the project as per estimation. If \npayment delayed by client, then completion time will vary, please make payment as per payment \nschedule subject to Bangalore city jurisdiction.  \n12. All works will execute as per Architectural & Structural drawings. If any changes made by client, \nit will be charged as per the rates.   \n13. 1 Year service on construction defects for mentioned works from SSC. Like Water \nblockage/Leakage from the taps, Electrical issues, Carpentry maintenance ETC."]}]};
